Title: FEDERAL TRACE
Episode: 102 "Parallel Construction"
Credit: Original fixture material written for the Canon AI test harness.

COLD OPEN

INT. FBI RIVERGATE FIELD OFFICE - BULLPEN - MORNING

The FT-401 board has doubled overnight. Red tags mark the dead source, the burned garage, and the missing case.

Priya writes TONER TRAY on the glass wall before Lena enters.

PRIYA
The spare key was taped under the copy-room toner tray because Nadia hid it there before the takedown.

MALIK
That detail was not in the 302.

PRIYA
It will be when the report catches up.

END COLD OPEN.

ACT ONE

INT. FEDERAL COURTHOUSE - WITNESS ROOM - DAY

AUSA NORA VENN, 40s, slides a subpoena packet across a bolted table to Malik.

NORA
Magistrate's order. You stay in this witness room until nine tonight. No hallway, no calls, no exceptions.

MALIK
I have an active kidnapping case.

NORA
You have a leak hearing. Pick the institution you want to save first.

The clerk locks the door from the outside.

INT. FBI EVIDENCE GARAGE - AFTERNOON

A wall clock reads 3:15 P.M.

The FBI Evidence Garage hums intact, fluorescent lights bright over clean evidence racks.

Malik steps between two evidence racks and signs a fresh chain-of-custody sheet.

MALIK
If anyone asks, this room never burned and I was never here.

ACT TWO

INT. FIELD OFFICE CONFERENCE ROOM - AFTERNOON

Keene, Lena, Priya, Darius, and Nora stare at the rail-yard access map.

Nadia stands at the monitor, dry coat, no wound, laser pointer in hand.

NADIA
You always catalog after the lie. That is how they own the truth.

Lena drops her pen.

LENA
Nadia?

Nadia smiles like the question is procedural.

NADIA
Start with the case number nobody opened.

INT. COMMAND CENTER - EVENING

Phones ring under a wall of camera feeds. Keene coordinates with JTTF while Lena scans license plates.

Darius pockets the encrypted drive and hands it to a janitor wearing no badge.

The janitor disappears through a service door before anyone looks up.

ACT THREE

INT. JTTF WAR ROOM - NIGHT

Federal partners crowd around a table: FBI, marshals, postal inspectors, courthouse security.

Keene tapes a redacted folder labeled CANTOR-19 to the inside of her case binder.

KEENE
Cantor stays sealed by court order. We do not brief it, speculate on it, or make it a theory.

LENA
Then what do we brief?

PRIYA
Sloane's burner just hit a camera two blocks from East Terminal.

Keene points to the tactical map.

KEENE
We have warrant predicate, live location, and a source down. Move on Sloane now.

EXT. EAST TERMINAL SERVICE PLATFORM - NIGHT

Rain hammers the platform. SWAT holds the stairwell. Lena and Keene approach VIKTOR SLOANE, 40s, courier jacket zipped to his chin.

SLOANE
I rented a car. That is not a federal conspiracy.

LENA
It is when the car moves stolen evidence and your burner pings the rail yard.

Sloane looks at the black sky above the tracks.

SLOANE
You are chasing the receipt. Sundial bought the store.

ACT FOUR

INT. FBI RIVERGATE FIELD OFFICE - BULLPEN - LATE NIGHT

The team returns soaked and silent. Sloane's booking photo prints from a laser printer.

Lena opens her notebook to the page marked CALDER? and then closes it before Malik can see.

MALIK
What did Nadia give you that you are not saying?

LENA
Enough to know this case is still open.

Keene watches them from her office doorway.

FADE OUT.
